WEBVTT

00:00:00.407 --> 00:00:04.640
Journey twenty-five: moderate reports and feature businesses.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.219
The Jubilee team handles the reports members send, and chooses the

00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:13.521
businesses featured this week. This run takes the journey from

00:00:13.521 --> 00:00:15.671
eighty-two percent to complete.

00:00:16.528 --> 00:00:19.676
A report must reach the team when it arrives.

00:00:19.676 --> 00:00:23.033
A report of a listing already e-mailed the team.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:28.068
Now a report of a conversation does too: New report, a conversation with

00:00:28.068 --> 00:00:32.684
the business, with what the member wrote and a link to the report.

00:00:32.684 --> 00:00:36.880
It never names who reported, and never carries the messages.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:41.192
Miriam of the Jubilee team opens the reports.

00:00:41.192 --> 00:00:46.489
Beside Reports, the admin bar now counts the unresolved reports, here

00:00:46.489 --> 00:00:50.097
two, and a screen reader hears: two unresolved.

00:00:50.799 --> 00:00:53.985
She opens the report about Luzandre dot com.

00:00:53.985 --> 00:00:59.198
Opening it moves it into review, and the access is recorded in the audit

00:00:59.198 --> 00:00:59.487
log.

00:01:00.188 --> 00:01:04.775
She places the listing on hold, with the note every action requires.

00:01:04.775 --> 00:01:09.295
The owner is told the listing is paused while the team looks into a

00:01:09.295 --> 00:01:11.588
report, and never who reported it.

00:01:12.618 --> 00:01:17.446
A held or removed listing leaves the welcome page, Browse, its category,

00:01:17.446 --> 00:01:21.403
search and the related businesses on the very next request.

00:01:21.403 --> 00:01:25.694
The save itself clears the directory cache, and search reads the

00:01:25.694 --> 00:01:28.242
database, so no outbox step is needed.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:34.343
Meanwhile another report comes in. The admin application does not poll,

00:01:34.343 --> 00:01:37.667
which would keep an idle staff session alive.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:42.983
It reads the staff session again each time Miriam moves between screens,

00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:44.460
or acts on a report.

00:01:45.162 --> 00:01:49.602
So when she opens the featured businesses, the bar reads three.

00:01:50.305 --> 00:01:54.645
She chooses this week's businesses, up to five live listings in the

00:01:54.645 --> 00:01:56.977
order she wants, and saves the week.

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:03.676
A week saved, or saved again, shows on the welcome page and Browse on

00:02:03.676 --> 00:02:08.657
the next request. A featured listing that is paused, held or removed is

00:02:08.657 --> 00:02:11.674
skipped, and returns when it is live again.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:17.583
Tests prove each criterion: API tests for the team's e-mail, the count

00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:22.562
and every public page, each seen failing first, and browser tests for

00:02:22.562 --> 00:02:23.572
the admin bar.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:29.876
Journey twenty-five is complete. Nothing new needs setting on Azure: the

00:02:29.876 --> 00:02:34.489
team's e-mail goes to the address already set for the launch.

00:02:34.489 --> 00:02:39.934
Left for the owner: run the visual, responsive and accessibility sweeps.
